  "term": "psychological model",
  "definition": "A psychological model is a structured way of showing how psychological experiences, perceptions, or traits are related to one another. In this source, it refers to a correlational model linking adolescents’ perceived educational experiences with resilience, rumination, emotional regulation, and perceived reduction in depressive symptoms.",
